    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>H2O2 model of the article: <strong>Selective oxidation of 3-hydroxypropionic acid to malonic acid over Pd/C: Mechanistic and kinetic study.</strong> Kim S.Y., Chavarrio J.E., Install J., Huber G.W. <i>Appl. Catal. B: Environ. Energy</i> 386 (2026) 126403. DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403">10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403</a></p>
        <p>Conditions: 60 mM 3-HP, 0.2 g 10 % Pd/C, NaOH/3-HP = 1:1, 15 equivalents of H2O2, 3 bar Ar, 50 C (Fig. 9a). The catalyst mass m_cat is the mass of the paper&apos;s batch (0.2 g), not a mass per litre. Rate constants: Table 3 (H2O2 column) as printed. Rate expressions: SI Fig. S2 with every order equal to 1 and unit activity coefficients. Seven first-order irreversible steps; the reaction orders and equilibrium constants of SI Table S4 are not used. </p>
        <p>Inferred from the authors&apos; data deposit (Dryad, DOI 10.5061/dryad.jsxksn0q4), which holds the model curve but only the O2 version of the script: H2O2 is a liquid state that enters reactions 1, 2 and 4 through its mole fraction on the authors&apos; scale (0.000339 per 60 mM) and is consumed 1:1 by each of them. </p>
        <p>The H2O2 curve of SI Fig. S12a (published inset and deposited trace) is not reproduced by the Table 3 constants: it lies up to 0.38 equivalents below this model (see NOTES.md). </p>
        <p>Only this one experiment was fitted; other values of m_cat, C0 or eq_H2O2_0 are extrapolations that were never compared with data. </p>
      </body>
